(*"approval_schema.approval"
An **approval** is a confirmation of the product data for its intended use. An **approval** is an incompletely modeled concept and requires population of related entity data types to form a complete approval.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval.__note"
The role of *approval* can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval.status"
the type or level of **approval** in terms of its usage.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval.status.__example"
One possible status is 'released for production'; this explicitly identifies the approved usage. Another possible status is 'preliminary design completed'; this only implies the approved usage that will depend upon company-specific procedures.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval.level"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> that provides a user interpretable designation for the level of completion of the approval.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_date_time"
An **approval_date_time** is an association between an <<express:approval_schema.approval,approval>> and a date, time, or date and time.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_date_time.date_time"
the moment when the **dated_approval** is given.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_date_time.dated_approval"
the <<express:approval_schema.approval,approval>> with which the date or time is associated.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_date_time.role"
the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.object_role,object_role>> that specifies the purpose of the association of the **approval_date_time** with product data.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_date_time.role.__note"
This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to *approval_date_time* as specified in ISO 10303-41:1994.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval_date_time.wr:WR1"
Each **approval_date_time** shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.role_association.item_with_role,item_with_role>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.role_association,role_association>>.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_date_time.wr:WR1.__note"
A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> is described in annex E.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval_person_organization"
An **approval_person_organization** is an association between an <<express:approval_schema.approval,approval>> and a given person, organization or person in the context of an organization.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_person_organization.person_organization"
the person or organization playing the given role.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_person_organization.authorized_approval"
the <<express:approval_schema.approval,approval>> that is effected by the person or organization.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_person_organization.role"
the <<express:approval_schema.approval_role,approval_role>> that specifies the purpose of the association of the <<express:approval_schema.approval,approval>> with a person or organization.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_relationship"
An **approval_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of the entity data type <<express:approval_schema.approval,approval>> with a description of their relationship.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_relationship.__note"
The role of *approval_relationship* can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval_relationship.__note"
This entity, together with the <<express:approval_schema.approval,approval>> entity, is based on the relationship template that is described in annex E.3.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **approval_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **approval_relationship**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_relationship.relating_approval"
one of the instances of <<express:approval_schema.approval,approval>> that is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_relationship.relating_approval.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval_relationship.related_approval"
the other instance of <<express:approval_schema.approval,approval>> that is a part of the relationship. If one element of the relationship is dependent upon the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_relationship.related_approval.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval_role"
An **approval_role** is a definition of a function. An **approval_role** is an incompletely modeled concept and requires population of related entity data types to form a complete confirmation.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_role.role"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **approval_role** is known.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_role.role.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval_role.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **approval_role**.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_role.description.__note"
This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to *approval_role* as specified in ISO 10303-41:1994.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval_role.wr:WR1"
Each **approval_role** shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute.described_item,described_item>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute,description_attribute>>.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_role.wr:WR1.__note"
The <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute,description_attribute>> data type is defined in <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> of this document.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval_role.wr:WR1.__note"
A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> is described in annex E.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval_status"
An **approval_status** specifies the state of an <<express:approval_schema.approval,approval>>.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval_status.__example"
'Approved' and 'disapproved' are examples of *approval_status*.
*)

(*"approval_schema.approval_status.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **approval_status** is known.
*)


(*"approval_schema.approval_status.name.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"approval_schema.acyclic_approval_relationship"
The **acyclic_approval_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:approval_schema.approval,approval>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either a <<express:approval_schema.approval_relationship,approval_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"approval_schema.acyclic_approval_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"approval_schema.acyclic_approval_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other ISO 10303 integrated resources and application protocols that use the <<express:approval_schema.approval_relationship,approval_relationship>> entity include rules that use this function.
*)

(*"approval_schema.acyclic_approval_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:approval_schema.approval_relationship,approval_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"approval_schema.acyclic_approval_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:approval_schema.approval,approval>> for which the function is searching in the <<express:approval_schema.approval_relationship.relating_approval,relating_approval>> parameter of the relation argument.
*)


(*"approval_schema.acyclic_approval_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified name of a subtype of the <<express:approval_schema.approval_relationship,approval_relationship>> entity.
*)


